cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use the Open Grid physics core, tyre-fitting tools or conformance suite in your work, please cite it as below."
title: "Open Grid: an open vehicle-dynamics core with a Magic Formula tyre evaluator, tyre-fitting tools and a conformance suite"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Chatzistavrou
    given-names: Konstantinos
    alias: Konstantinos-Chatzistavrou
repository-code: "https://github.com/Konstantinos-Chatzistavrou/Open-Grid"
url: "https://open-grid.racing/"
license: Apache-2.0
abstract: >-
  Open Grid is an open-source motorsport simulator. Its engine-independent C++20 physics core includes a
  Pacejka Magic Formula 5.2 / 6.1 / 6.2 tyre evaluator that is checked against the MFeval reference
  implementation, a tool that fits tyre property files to measured curves, a generator and checker for
  car files, and a file-based conformance suite that other simulations can run.
keywords:
  - vehicle dynamics
  - Pacejka Magic Formula
  - tyre model
  - racing simulation
  - conformance testing
